REGENT OF PASANGKAYU
WEST SULAWESI PROVINCE
REGIONAL REGULATION OF PASANGKAYU REGENCY NUMBER 9 OF 2019
CONCERNING
PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
REGENT OF PASANGKAYU,
Considering : a. that women and children are creations of Almighty God who constitute important elements of society and the Indonesian Nation;
b. that in the life of society, women and children often experience violence or unpleasant treatment;
c. that all forms of violence against women and children constitute violations of human rights so that their dignity and honor need to be protected and their right to life guaranteed in accordance with their nature and natural disposition without discrimination;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Protection of Women and Children.
In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 7 of 2003 concerning the Establishment of East Luwu Regency and North Mamuju Regency in South Sulawesi Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2003 Number 27, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4270);
3. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette

text:
JDIH KABUPATEN PASANGKAYU
a. memberikan dan meningkatkan rasa aman bagi Perempuan  dan Anak;
b. membantu mencegah tindak Kekerasan terhadap Perempuan  dan Anak;
c. membantu mencegah kegiatan eksploitasi terhadap  Perempuan dan Anak.
d. memberikan Pelayanan kepada Perempuan dan Anak dalam  menghadapi permasalahan hukum; dan
e. membantu meningkatkan kualitas hidup Perempuan dan  Anak.

translated_text:
JDIH KABUPATEN PASANGKAYU
a. provide and enhance a sense of security for Women and Children;
b. help prevent acts of Violence against Women and Children;
c. help prevent exploitation activities against Women and Children;
d. provide Services to Women and Children in facing legal problems; and
e. help improve the quality of life of Women and Children.

text:
Pasal 3
Ruang lingkup pengaturan dalam Peraturan Daerah ini meliputi:  a. bentuk-bentuk Kekerasan;
b. hak-hak Perempuan dan Anak;
c. tugas dan wewenang;
d. penanganan tindak Kekerasan;
e. pendanaan;
f. pembinaan dan pengawasan; dan
g. peran serta masyarakat.

translated_text:
Article 3
The scope of regulation in this Regional Regulation includes:
a. forms of Violence;
b. rights of Women and Children;
c. duties and authorities;
d. handling of acts of Violence;
e. funding;
f. guidance and supervision; and
g. community participation.

text:
BAB III
BENTUK-BENTUK KEKERASAN
Pasal 4
Bentuk-bentuk kekerasan terhadap Perempuan dan Anak berupa:
a. Kekerasan fisik;
b. Kekerasan psikis;
c. Kekerasan seksual;
d. penelantaran; dan/atau
e. eksploitasi.

translated_text:
CHAPTER III
FORMS OF VIOLENCE
Article 4
Forms of violence against Women and Children consist of:
a. Physical violence;
b. Psychological violence;
c. Sexual violence;
d. neglect; and/or
e. exploitation.

text:
Pasal 8
Penelantaran sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 4 huruf d  disebabkan karena:
a. perbuatan yang mengakibatkan tidak terpenuhinya  kebutuhan Anak secara wajar, baik fisik, mental, spiritual  maupun sosial yang dilakukan oleh orang tua, wali, atau  pihak lain yang bertanggung jawab atas pengasuhan;
b. perbuatan mengabaikan dengan sengaja untuk memelihara,  merawat, atau mengurus Anak sebagaimana mestinya yang  dilakukan oleh orang tua, wali atau pihak lain yang bertanggung jawab atas pengasuhannya;
c. perbuatan yang menelantarkan orang dalam lingkup rumah  tangganya, padahal menurut hukum yang berlaku baginya  atau karena persetujuan atau perjanjian wajib memberikan  penghidupan, perawatan, atau pemeliharaan kepada orang  tersebut; dan/atau
d. perbuatan yang mengakibatkan ketergantungan ekonomi dengan cara membatasi dan/atau melarang untuk bekerja

translated_text:
Article 8
Neglect as referred to in Article 4 letter d is caused by:
a. acts that result in the failure to fulfill the needs of the Child properly, whether physical, mental, spiritual or social, committed by parents, guardians, or other parties responsible for care;
b. acts of deliberately neglecting to maintain, care for, or look after the Child as appropriate, committed by parents, guardians or other parties responsible for their care;
c. acts of neglecting a person within the household scope, whereas according to the law applicable to the perpetrator or due to an agreement or contract, the perpetrator is obliged to provide livelihood, care, or maintenance to that person; and/or
d. acts that result in economic dependence by means of restricting and/or prohibiting from working

text:
Pasal 10
(1) Pemerintah Daerah wajib melindungi hak Perempuan di Daerah.
(2) Hak Perempuan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) berupa  hak atas:
a. kebutuhan dasar;
b. rasa nyaman dan rasa aman;
c. Pelayanan kesehatan maksimal dalam menghadapi  tindak Kekerasan;
d. layanan pendampingan, bantuan hukum dan bimbingan  rohani dalam menghadapi tindak Kekerasan; dan  e. kerahasiaan atas masalah yang dihadapi.

translated_text:
Article 10
(1) Regional Governments are obligated to protect the rights of Women in the Region.
(2) The rights of Women as referred to in paragraph (1) consist of the right to:
a. basic needs;
b. comfort and security;
c. maximum health services in facing acts of Violence;
d. assistance services, legal aid and spiritual guidance in facing acts of Violence; and
e. confidentiality regarding the problems faced.

text:
JDIH KABUPATEN PASANGKAYU
Pasal 11
(1) Pemerintah Daerah wajib melindungi hak Anak di Daerah.  (2) Hak Anak sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) berupa hak  untuk:
a. dapat hidup, tumbuh, berkembang dan berpartisipasi  secara wajar sesuai dengan harkat dan martabat  kemanusiaan serta mendapat pembinaan dan  Perlindungan dari Kekerasan dan diskriminasi;
b. beribadah menurut agamanya, berpikir dan berekspresi  sesuai dengan tingkat kecerdasan dan usianya dalam  bimbingan orang tua;
c. suatu akta kelahiran yang diperoleh dan/atau diusahakan  oleh orang tuanya sesuai dengan ketentuan peraturan perundang-undangan yang berlaku;
d. mendapatkan perlindungan dari keluarga, masyarakat  dan Pemerintah Daerah terhadap perlakuan diskriminasi  dan eksploitasi baik secara ekonomi maupun sosial,  penelantaran, kekejaman, kekerasan, penganiayaan,  ketidak-adilan dan perlakuan salah lainnya;
e. mendapatkan kembali pendidikan formal atau nonformal  bagi Anak putus sekolah;
f. memperoleh Pelayanan kesehatan dan jaminan sosial  sesuai dengan kebutuhan fisik, mental spritual dan sosial;  g. memperoleh pendidikan dan pengajaran sesuai  kemampuan, minat dan bakatnya; dan
h. memperoleh hak lainnya sesuai dengan ketentuan  peraturan perundang-undangan.

translated_text:
JDIH KABUPATEN PASANGKAYU
Article 11
(1) The Regional Government is obligated to protect the rights of Children in the Region.
(2) The rights of Children as referred to in paragraph (1) consist of the right to:
a. live, grow, develop and participate appropriately in accordance with human dignity and worth and receive guidance and Protection from Violence and discrimination;
b. worship according to their religion, think and express themselves in accordance with their level of intelligence and age under parental guidance;
c. a birth certificate obtained and/or procured by their parents in accordance with the provisions of applicable laws and regulations;
d. obtain protection from family, community and Regional Government against discriminatory treatment and exploitation both economically and socially, neglect, cruelty, violence, abuse, injustice and other mistreatment;
e. regain formal or non-formal education for Children who have dropped out of school;
f. obtain health Services and social security in accordance with physical, mental, spiritual and social needs;
g. obtain education and teaching in accordance with their abilities, interests and talents; and
h. obtain other rights in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

text:
Pasal 21
(1) Pemerintah Daerah wajib melakukan pencegahan atas upaya  dan tindakan kekerasan terhadap Anak.
(2) Upaya pencegahan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilakukan dengan bentuk kegiatan yang meliputi:  a. deteksi dan intervensi dini;
b. sosialisasi, seminar atau lokakarya;
c. penyiapan sistem informasi yang efektif; dan
d. kerja sama dengan lembaga yang mempunyai kegiatan  dalam pencegahan tindak kekerasan terhadap Anak.

Pasal 27
